  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the late 19th century, as industrialization rapidly transformed Europe and America, a new social movement emerged. The socialists' vision was to create an equal society where everyone would have access to basic needs like food, shelter, and education. They believed that the wealth generated by industry should be distributed fairly among all citizens rather than concentrated in the hands of a few. However, their ideas were met with significant opposition from those who saw socialism as a threat to personal freedom and capitalist principles.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was the main goal of socialist movement during the late 19th century?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"To promote economic growth\",\n        \"To create an equal society with shared wealth\",\n        \"To protect individual freedoms from government interference\",\n        \"To centralize all industries under state control\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following statements best describes socialist belief in distributing wealth?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It should be given to those who need it most\",\n        \"It should be concentrated in the hands of a few elites\",\n        \"It should be distributed equally among all citizens\",\n        \"It should be used to support artistic and cultural endeavors\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What was a primary reason for opposition to socialist ideas?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"They were seen as unworkable in modern times\",\n        \"People feared losing their personal freedoms\",\n        \"Socialists did not have a clear plan for economic reform\",\n        \"They were too focused on environmental conservation\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following statements is true about socialist beliefs regarding industry?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"They opposed any form of government intervention in industries\",\n        \"They wanted to control all industries through the state\",\n        \"They believed that wealth generated by industry should be shared fairly\",\n        \"They advocated for complete privatization of all industries\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author's attitude towards socialism from this passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"They are sympathetic to socialist ideals\",\n        \"They display a neutral viewpoint\",\n        \"They express skepticism towards the movement\",\n        \"They advocate for socialist policies\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
